Candidate namespace seccomp policy

Derived from the Moby default seccomp profile distributed in Moby v28.5.1,
commit f8215cc266744ef195a50a70d427c345da2acdbb,
vendor/github.com/moby/profiles/seccomp/default.json (module v0.1.0).
Upstream source: https://github.com/moby/moby
License: Apache License, Version 2.0; retained in candidate-policy.LICENSE.
The exact unmodified baseline is retained in the development policy packet.

Local changes: eleven arm64-only allow rules appended to the baseline rules.
They permit unshare flags 1879179264; mount flags 278528, 20480, 6, 4096,
4134, 2, 4131, 4135, or 14; and mount_setattr flags 32768 with size 32.
No new umount2 permission is added. Remaining baseline semantics are held.

These rules compare scalar syscall arguments. They cannot inspect pointed
pathnames, filesystem types, mount data, or mount_attr contents. Kernel user
namespace ownership, LSM restrictions, and the held engine validation,
capability reduction, and IPC barriers remain essential.

Use only for the selected candidate role. Keep outer CapDrop ALL,
no-new-privileges, nonroot user, read-only root, and network none. This is a
source-audited proposed policy; Docker, unshare, native admission, and hardware
execution were not run. The actual EPERM denier remains unknown.
